irls that all children have to  learn to try and fail and try again  and like struggle through humiliation  and figure  and go through it again all the time  knowing that a parent or a friend is  loving and caring and supportive of them  all the time and I think that's the  essential part which is there's always  someone who's there who loves me because  the only way we get courage I for one  believe courage is an external thing not  an internal thing you know the reason we  jump out of a plane is not because of  some deep internal fortitude is because  there's a parachute in our back  it's the parachute that gave us the  courage I've you know many people in  this room you haven't you know men or  women who have risked their live lives  to save the life of somebody else  thinking they were gonna die and through  some miracle survived and we've I've  asked them I've asked I've asked them  why'd you do it  you've got a family you've got kids no  one or did you do it no one would have  would have ordered you to do it no one  would have faulted you if you didn't do  it you may have even violent you know  disobeyed an order to do it you know  why'd you do it  and they say they almost all say the  same thing which is I did it because  they would have done it for me the  courage comes from the confidence that  somebody else has my back  and that's what gives me the confidence  to do things even though I'm scared and  so it goes back to those human  relationships as long as a child knows  that there's someone there who loves me  then we should allow them to go through  those very difficult frustrating and  uncomfortable  [Music]
 

